Firmware: ODROID-C5 bootloader: Amlogic's boot stages (BL2 and the stages it
          loads, BL30, BL31 and BL32, signed and encrypted for the S905X5M)
          and Hardkernel's U-Boot (BL33)
Hardware: Hardkernel ODROID-C5 (Amlogic S905X5M, SoC family S7D) only
Files:    the SD card's sectors 1 to 6538, written by the image build; the
          root file system has only Amlogic's license, the GPL-2 text of
          U-Boot and this notice below
          /usr/share/licenses/amlogic-s7d-bootloader, and the manifest
Source:   Hardkernel's official ODROID-C5 image
          ubuntu-22.04-gnome-desktop-odroidc5-20260610-bsp-boot.img.xz
          (37760380 bytes, SHA-256
          04b9817d4e5e27ac4cc46dc4ad48fbc164e9a6c6f42eb1b0ba8d7a927accc5f2),
          kept unmodified in the zedBSD firmware repository
          https://github.com/awemorris/zedBSD-firmware (amlogic-s7d/), with
          LICENSE.amlogic (1273 bytes, SHA-256
          5e8f7ad650a0af4a14ad5641817323f654d0e1b8dc2019aa6f0944ba9108ff65).
          The build decompresses the image and takes its sectors 1 to 6538
          (3347456 bytes, SHA-256
          6c5316ed320c78c9c2a67665cdee1089339be25bee625cf1eaffb0a6277c6562;
          the BL30 in it names itself S7D-s905x5m-26052812).

Copyright (C) 2018 Amlogic, Inc. (the boot stages BL2 to BL32)
Copyright the U-Boot authors and Hardkernel Co., Ltd. (U-Boot)

Terms:
- Amlogic's boot stages are under Amlogic's license (LICENSE.amlogic): they
  are provided under a Software License Agreement with Amlogic, and
  redistribution and use without Amlogic's prior written permission are
  prohibited.  Amlogic has given that permission to Hardkernel, which
  distributes them in its images for the ODROID-C5, and such an image, which
  can be used only on this board, may be redistributed.  So use them only on
  a Hardkernel ODROID-C5, and pass them on (for example in an SD card image
  made with this package) only unmodified, with LICENSE.amlogic and this
  notice, and only for use on the ODROID-C5.
- U-Boot is under the GNU General Public License version 2 or later (the
  text: GPL-2 beside this notice, from linux-firmware commit
  dc85ccedc9c973682fbcf4d628ca61174bcc3120, 18092 bytes, SHA-256
  8177f97513213526df2cf6184d8ff986c675afb514d4e68a404010521b880643).  Its
  corresponding source is Hardkernel's: the submodule bl33/v2023 of the
  branch odroidc5-v2023.01 of https://github.com/hardkernel/u-boot (commit
  c99f3409d5cad031b365fd871e543f97af893f88), on
  https://git.odroid.com/yocto/uboot.  zedBSD changes nothing in it.
- The boot ROM accepts only stages signed for the S905X5M, so the area is
  written as it is; zedBSD does not modify, re-sign or rebuild it.

Without the firmware repository: a build cannot fetch the image from
Hardkernel.  Download it from Hardkernel's ODROID-C5 page yourself, and place
it, under its own name, with LICENSE.amlogic (the text in the firmware
repository's amlogic-s7d/), in build/sources/firmware/amlogic-s7d/by-hand/
(or AMLOGIC_S7D_BOOTLOADER_CACHE_ROOT/by-hand/).  The build then asks about
the license and checks the same sizes and SHA-256 values.
